A ternary search algorithm is a divide and conquer algorithm that can be used to find an element in an array. It is similar to binary search where we divide the array into two parts but in ternary search we divide the given array into three parts and determine which has the key.

Below is a Python solution:

```python
def ternarySearch(arr, l, r, x):
    if r >= l:
        mid1 = l + (r-l) // 3
        mid2 = r - (r-l) // 3
        if arr[mid1] == x:
            return mid1
        if arr[mid2] == x:
            return mid2
        if x < arr[mid1]:
            return ternarySearch(l, mid1-1, x)
        elif x > arr[mid2]:
            return ternarySearch(mid2+1, r, x)
        else:
            return ternarySearch(mid1+1, mid2-1, x)
    return -1

