{
  [BreakBuild("This method will break the build.")]
  public void DoSomething()
  {
    // Some code here.
  }
}
```

However, unless you have some other piece of code in your build process that's specifically looking for the presence of `[BreakBuild]` attributes via reflection, all this will do is decorate the `DoSomething` method with some additional metadata - it won't break the build.

To implement code that causes the build to break when this attribute is present, you would need to create some sort of tool (like a Roslyn analyzer) that looks for this attribute and fail the build process if it's found. But that would be a separate tool you'd have to create and integrate with your build process.

