2. `is_twin_prime(n)` checks if a number `n` and `n + 2` are both prime numbers. If they are, then they form a twin prime.

3. `least_common_multiple(limit)` calculates the least common multiple (LCM) of all prime numbers up to a given `limit`, excluding twin primes. It finds each prime number `i` up to the limit, checks if it is not part of a twin prime pair (i.e., `i + 2` is not prime), and if it isn't, then `i` is included in the LCM calculation by multiplying `lcm` by `i`.

