Yes, ASP.NET MVC does support nested controller directories and namespaces. This organization of controllers helps to manage the complexity of a large project into more manageable parts.

To get this structure working, you have to reflect your directory structure in the namespaces of your controllers, and then create routes that understand these namespaces.

For example, if you have a "Controllers/Warehouse/Supplies/" directory, the SuppliesController inside it would look like this:

```csharp
namespace YourAppName.Controllers.Warehouse.Supplies
{
