```java
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.Iterator;
import java.util.LinkedList;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        LinkedList<Integer> values = new LinkedList<>(Arrays.asList(3, 6, 12, 24, 48));

        int curValue = 50;
        Iterator<Integer> iterator = values.descendingIterator();
        while (iterator.hasNext()) {
            Integer value = iterator.next();

            // Insert all the curValue down to the next value from the list
            while (curValue > value) {
                values.addFirst(curValue);
                // decrement the inserted values by 1
                curValue--;
            }
        }

        // Insert remaining curValue down to 2
        while (curValue >= 2) {
            values.addFirst(curValue);
            curValue--;
        }

        // Printing the final LinkedList
        for (Integer val : values) {
            System.out.println(val);
        }
    }
}
```

This program adds values to the `LinkedList` in descending order from 50 to 2. It makes use of the `descendingIterator` function of `LinkedList` to efficiently loop through the given list in reverse order and every time the `curValue` is greater than the current value of `LinkedList`, it adds it to the list.

In terms of performance, this solution is quite efficient making it in constant time O(1) while modifying `LinkedList`. Though, there is a loop inside the loop, both loops essentially iterate through each element of Linked list only once. Therefore, it is O(n) in terms of runtime where 'n' is the number of elements in the list.

As for its thread safety, this java program is not thread safe. If multiple threads were trying to add elements to the `LinkedList` at the same time, it could lead to race condition and hence data inconsistency. To make it thread safe, you could consider using `Collections.synchronizedList(new LinkedList<>(Arrays.asList(3, 6, 12, 24, 48)));` which will make this LinkedList synchronized and thread-safe. But remember, iterator should be used in synchronous block even when it is created for synchronized list. 

