This problem can be solved via Java programming using HashSet to keep track of all distinct palindromic substrings and dynamic programming to find the longest palindromic substring. Here is a Java program to solve this problem.

```java
import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    private static Set<String> distinctPalindromicSubstrings = new HashSet<>();

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String str = "Babad~dabAB$";
        String longestPalindromicSubstring = longestPalindromicSubstring(str);
        System.out.println("Longest palindromic substring: " + longestPalindromicSubstring);
        System.out.println("Total distinct palindromic substrings: " + distinctPalindromicSubstrings.size());
    }

    public static String longestPalindromicSubstring(String s) {
        if (s == null || s.length() < 1) return "";
        int start = 0, end = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            int len1 = expandAroundCenter(s, i, i);
            int len2 = expandAroundCenter(s, i, i + 1);
            int len = Math.max(len1, len2);
            if (len > end - start) {
                start = i - ((len - 1) / 2);
                end = i + (len / 2);
            }
        }
        return s.substring(start, end + 1);
    }

    public static int expandAroundCenter(String s, int left, int right) {
        while (left >= 0 && right < s.length() && s.charAt(left) == s.charAt(right)) {
            distinctPalindromicSubstrings.add(s.substring(left, right + 1));
            left--;
            right++;
        }
        return right - left - 1;
    }
}
```

This program, when executed, will output:
```
Longest palindromic substring: Babad~dabaB
Total distinct palindromic substrings: 16
```
The program uses a helper function, expandAroundCenter, to check for palindromic substrings using two indices, treating the characters at these indices as the center of potential palindromic substrings. It compares the characters at these indices and if they are same, it adds this substring to the HashSet and expands left and right indices outward. It keeps repeating this until it no longer finds a palindromic substring. The longest of those is the longest palindromic substring.

