PHP does not have a built-in Unicode database like Python, so it does not have a PHP equivalent to Python's `unicodedata.normalize()`. Therefore, different approaches can be implemented, the following is an implementation using `Normalizer::normalize()` from PHP's intl extension:

```php
<?php
function subtilized_vowel_counter($s)
{
    $vowels = 'aeiouyAEIOUY';
    $diacritics = '\u0300\u0301\u0302\u0308'; // includes grave, acute, circumflex and diaeresis
    $count = 0;

    $normalized = Normalizer::normalize($s, Normalizer::FORM_D);

    for ($i = 0; $i < mb_strlen($normalized); $i++)
    {
        $char = mb_substr($normalized, $i, 1);

        if (strpos($vowels, $char) !== false)
        {
            if (mb_strtolower($char) != 'y' || $i == mb_strlen($normalized) - 1 || strpos($diacritics, mb_substr($normalized, $i + 1, 1)) === false)
            {
                $count++;
            }
        }
        elseif (strpos($diacritics, $char) !== false)
        {
            if ($i == 0 || strpos($vowels, mb_substr($normalized, $i - 1, 1)) === false)
            {
                $count++;
            }
        }
    }

    return $count;
}
?>
```

Please note that PHP's intl and mbstring extensions need to be enabled for this code to work. 

