Here is a simple class representation of the AVL tree:

```php
class AVLNode {
    public $key;
    public $left;
    public $right;
    public $height;

    public function __construct($key) {
        $this->key = $key;
        $this->left = null;
        $this->right = null;
        $this->height = 1;
    }
}

class AVLTree {
    private $root;

    private function height($node) {
        if($node == null)
            return 0;
        return $node->height;
    }

    private function rotateRight($y) {
        $x = $y->left;
        $T2 = $x->right;

        $x->right = $y;
        $y->left = $T2;

        $y->height = max($this->height($y->left), $this->height($y->right)) + 1;
        $x->height = max($this->height($x->left), $this->height($x->right)) + 1;

        return $x;
    }

    private function rotateLeft($y) {
        $x = $y->right;
        $T2 = $x->left;

        $x->left = $y;
        $y->right = $T2;

        $y->height = max($this->height($y->left), $this->height($y->right)) + 1;
        $x->height = max($this->height($x->left), $this->height($x->right)) + 1;

        return $x;
    }

    private function balance($node) {
        if($node == null)
            return 0;
        return $this->height($node->left) - $this->height($node->right);
    }

    public function insert($key) {
        $this->root = $this->insertNode($this->root, $key);
    }

    private function insertNode($node, $key) {
        if($node == null)
            return new AVLNode($key);

        if(strcmp($key, $node->key)<0)
            $node->left = $this->insertNode($node->left, $key);
        else if(strcmp($key, $node->key)>0)
            $node->right = $this->insertNode($node->right, $key);
        else
            return $node;

        $node->height = 1 + max($this->height($node->left), $this->height($node->right));

        $balance = $this->balance($node);

        if($balance > 1 && strcmp($key, $node->left->key)<0)
            return $this->rotateRight($node);

        if($balance < -1 && strcmp($key, $node->right->key)>0)
            return $this->rotateLeft($node);

        if($balance > 1 && strcmp($key, $node->left->key)>0) {
            $node->left = $this->rotateLeft($node->left);
            return $this->rotateRight($node);
        }

        if($balance < -1 && strcmp($key, $node->right->key)<0) {
            $node->right = $this->rotateRight($node->right);
            return $this->rotateLeft($node);
        }

        return $node;
    }

    // Similar methods for delete and search operations should also be implemented.
}
```

In this code:

- The `AVLNode` class represents a node in the AVL tree, storing the key, left child, right child and the height of the node.
- The `AVLTree` class represents the AVL tree itself, containing methods for insertion, rotation, and balance checking.

