Here's a Python program that solves the problem based on QuickSelect algorithm, a selection algorithm to find the k-th smallest element in an unordered list or array. It only partially sorts the data and completely eliminates built-in methods or functions:

```python
def partition(l, low, high, cmp_func):
    pivot = l[high]
    i = (low - 1)

    for j in range(low, high):
        if cmp_func(l[j], pivot) < 0:
            i = i + 1
            l[i], l[j] = l[j], l[i]
    l[i + 1], l[high] = l[high], l[i + 1]
    return (i + 1)

def quick_select(l, low, high, k, cmp_func):
    if (k > 0 and k <= high - low + 1):
        index = partition(l, low, high, cmp_func)

        if (index - low == k - 1):
            return l[index]
        if (index - low > k - 1):
            return quick_select(l, low, index - 1, k, cmp_func)

        return quick_select(l, index + 1, high, k - index + low - 1, cmp_func)

    return float('inf')

def customized_median(l, cmp_func):
    n = len(l)
    if n % 2 == 0:
        return (quick_select(l, 0, n - 1, n // 2, cmp_func) +
                quick_select(l, 0, n - 1, n // 2 + 1, cmp_func)) / 2.0
    else:
        return quick_select(l, 0, n - 1, n // 2 + 1, cmp_func)

print(customized_median([1, 2, 3, 200, 300, 400, 500], lambda a, b: a - b))
print(customized_median([-100, 10, 20, 30, 1000], lambda a, b: a - b))
print(customized_median([1, 2, 3, 3, 5], lambda a, b: a - b))
```
This solves the problem as you wanted. If we require to find a particular element in an array, doing so by sorting the array first will be pretty inefficient. In such cases, we use selection-based algorithms. Quick select operates similarly to quick sort, but instead of recursing into both sides, it only recurses into one side – the side with the element it is searching for, which saves a considerable amount of time, making the time complexity to O(n) in average case and O(n^2) in worst case.

This program could be useful in situations where you need to calculate median, especially when it is required to maintain the original order of data since it does not sort the complete data but partially sorts the data only based on the index position. However, make sure your data does not have too many repeated elements which can make worst case scenario for this algorithm same as the worst case for Quick sort.

