2. Invoking constructors: Inside `Person()`, `this("No Name")` is used to invoke the other constructor `Person(String name)`. This helps in avoiding code duplication.

3. Passing the current instance as an argument: Inside `Person(String name)`, `greet(this)` is used to pass the current instance as an argument. The keyword `this` allows methods to access and modify the instance that invoked them.

Not using "this" when needed could lead to errors and confusion. For example, in the setter method `setName(String name)`, if "this" is not used, the method parameter `name` will essentially shadow the instance variable `name`. Not using the keyword "this" here would mean that the instance variable is not being set, leading to possible bugs in your program. It can also lead to confusion for other developers reading the code, who might misinterpret which variable is being referred to in a given context.

