&lt;img src=&#34;resources/images/0716_gridgraphics.jpg?1678992054&#34; class=&#34;dark_img&#34; alt=&#34;&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
Let's define $C(H,W)$ as the sum of $S(\mathcal{G})$ for all potential graphs on a grid of $H\times W$. You are provided with $C(3,3) = 408$, $C(3,6) = 4696$ and $C(10,20) \equiv 988971143 \pmod{1\,000\,000\,007}$.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
Your task is to determine $C(10\,000,20\,000)$, providing your answer modulo $1\,000\,000\,007$.
