public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] numericArray = { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };
        int k = 2;
        circularShift(numericArray, k);
        for (int i : numericArray) {
            System.out.print(i + " ");
        }
    }

    public static void circularShift(int[] array, int k) {
        int n = array.length;
        reverseArray(array, 0, n-1);
        reverseArray(array, 0, k-1);
        reverseArray(array, k, n-1);
    }

    public static void reverseArray(int[] arr, int start, int end) {
        int temp;
        while(start < end){
            temp = arr[start];
            arr[start] = arr[end];
            arr[end] = temp;
            start++;
            end--;
        }
    }
}
```

This will also result in the output: `4 5 1 2 3`.

Please note that the displacement direction is from right to left. Therefore, 'k' displacement of 2 means the last two elements are moved to the beginning. If the direction were from left to right, we would need to adjust the code accordingly.

