This Python code is simulating a racing game with left and right lanes. The cars are moving from one end to another at different speeds. If a collision happens between a car from the left lane and a car from the right lane, they will move together at a new speed (after_collision_speed). The function `advanced_car_race_collision` is used to calculate the time of the first event that no car's front is behind another car's back.

Below is the Swift equivalent:

