import java.util.regex.Matcher;
import java.util.regex.Pattern;

public class WalletValidator {
    private static final Pattern bitcoinPattern = Pattern.compile("^[13][a-km-zA-HJ-NP-Z1-9]{25,34}$|^bc1[a-zA-HJ-NP-Z0-9]{25,39}$");
    private static final Pattern ethereumPattern = Pattern.compile("^0x[a-fA-F0-9]{40}$");
    private static final Pattern litecoinPattern = Pattern.compile("^[LM3][a-km-zA-HJ-NP-Z1-9]{25,34}$|^ltc1[a-zA-HJ-NP-Z0-9]{25,39}$");

    public static String validateWalletAddress(String walletAddress) {
        Matcher bitcoinMatcher = bitcoinPattern.matcher(walletAddress);
        Matcher ethereumMatcher = ethereumPattern.matcher(walletAddress);
        Matcher litecoinMatcher = litecoinPattern.matcher(walletAddress);

        if (bitcoinMatcher.find()) {
            return "Bitcoin wallet address is valid";
        } else if (ethereumMatcher.find()) {
            return "Ethereum wallet address is valid";
        } else if (litecoinMatcher.find()) {
            return "Litecoin wallet address is valid";
        } else {
            return "Wallet address is not valid for Bitcoin, Ethereum or Litecoin";
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(validateWalletAddress("1A1zP1eP5QGefi2DMPTfTL5SLmv7DivfNa")); // Expected output: Bitcoin wallet address is valid
        System.out.println(validateWalletAddress("0x742d35Cc6634C0532925a3b844Bc454e4438f44e")); // Expected output: Ethereum wallet address is valid
        System.out.println(validateWalletAddress("LdP8Qox1VAhCzLJNqrr74YovaWYyNBUWvL")); // Expected output: Litecoin wallet address is valid
        System.out.println(validateWalletAddress("InvalidAddress")); // Expected output: Wallet address is not valid for Bitcoin, Ethereum or Litecoin
    }
}
```

In the above code:
- `Pattern.compile()` compiles the regular expression into a pattern.
- `.matcher(walletAddress)` creates a matcher for the compiled pattern for the given wallet address.
- The `Matcher` object's `.find()` function then checks if the regular expression can be found within the given string. If it is, that means the wallet address matches the rules for that type of cryptocurrency (Bitcoin, Ethereum or Litecoin).

