Remember, UNIX timestamp is the number of seconds that have passed since Thursday, January 1, 1970 00:00:00 UTC minus the leap seconds. Because of this, it's a widely used time format in computing.

Also note that the port number (8080 in this example) can be any valid port number, but if you choose a port number below 1024, you may need special permissions to start the server.

