You should be using server-side pagination with virtual scrolling in this case. This means that you don't load all 100k records at once, but you load them in small chunks as you scroll down.

The 'ng-table-virtual-scroll' package doesn't support server-side pagination out of the box, but you can implement it manually. You will need to listen scroll events and when your table is close to the bottom you should load next chunk of data from the backend.

This is a rough example of how it can be implemented:

```
import { VirtualScrollDatasource } from 'ng-table-virtual-scroll';

class MyDataSource extends VirtualScrollDatasource<any> {
  actualDataSize = 100000; // Real amount of data in your database. Get it from server.
  currentPage = 0;
  pageSize = 100; // How much data you want to load each time. Tune this value for your needs.

  requestData(index: number, count: number): Observable<any[]> {
    if (this.shouldLoadMoreData(index)) {
      this.currentPage++;
      this.loadDataFromBackend(this.currentPage, this.pageSize);
    }
    return super.requestData(index, count);
  }

  private shouldLoadMoreData(index: number): boolean {
    const visibleDataSize = this.pageSize * this.currentPage;
    const almostScrolledToBottom = index > 0.7 * visibleDataSize;
    const canLoadMoreData = visibleDataSize < this.actualDataSize;
    return almostScrolledToBottom && canLoadMoreData;
  }

  private loadDataFromBackend(page: number, count: number): void {
    yourBackendService.getData(page, count).subscribe(
      (data) => {
        this.data.push(...data);
        this.dataSubject.next(this.data);  
      }  
    );
  }
}
```

