Symmetric text sequence is a sequence that reads the same forwards as backwards, like "abcba" or "1221". Here are the steps to verify the symmetric nature of a text sequence in C#:

Step 1:
Start the C# programming environment.

Step 2: 
Create a method that accepts a string parameter (the text sequence to be tested). 

Sample code:
```C#
public static bool IsSymmetric(string sequence)
{
    // Code to verify if the text sequence is symmetric
}
```

Step 3:
Within the method, initialize two integer variables. Let one variable (start) be the starting index of the sequence (which will be 0), and the other variable (end) be the last index (which is generally the length of the string – 1).

Sample code:
```C#
int start = 0;
int end = sequence.Length - 1;
```

Step 4:
Set up a loop that runs as long as the start index is less than or equal to the end index.

Sample code:
```C#
while (start <= end)
{
    // Code to be executed
}
```

Step 5:
Inside the loop, check if the characters at the start and end indices of the string are the same. If they aren't- the sequence can’t be symmetric, so return false. 

If they are the same, increment the start index by 1 and decrement the end index by 1.

Sample code:
```C#
while (start <= end)
{
    if (sequence[start] != sequence[end])
    {
        return false;
    }
    start++;
    end--;
}
```

Step 6:
If the loop completes (i.e., you’ve checked all the pairs of characters from  outside towards the center of the sequence) and you haven’t returned false, the sequence is symmetric, so you can return true.

Sample code:
```C#
return true;
```

Complete Code:
```C#
public static bool IsSymmetric(string sequence)
{
    int start = 0;
    int end = sequence.Length - 1;

    while (start <= end)
    {
        if (sequence[start] != sequence[end])
        {
            return false;
        }
        start++;
        end--;
    }

    return true;
}
```
You can hence call this function with the string input that needs to be tested for symmetry as:
```C#
Console.WriteLine(IsSymmetric("abcba")); // Returns true
Console.WriteLine(IsSymmetric("abcdefg")); // Returns false
```

