The function 'longestRepeatingSubstring' uses dynamic programming to find the longest repeating substring in the given string. It starts by creating an empty matrix (2D array). Each cell in the matrix is initialized to 0. Then it iteratively fills in the matrix such that dp[i+1][j+1] contains the length of repeating characters between s[0..i] and s[0..j] (excluding s[i] and s[j]). 

While filling in the table, it also keeps track of the max length of repeating string and the ending position of the repeating string in the hashmap. After the table is built, if the max length is greater than 0, it uses the substring function to extract the repeating string from the given string.

```javascript
function longestRepeatingSubstring(str) {
  let n = str.length;
  let dp = Array.from(Array(n+1), () => new Array(n+1).fill(0));
  let maxLen = 0;
  let end = 0;
  let lenTemp = 0;
  let hashMap = {};

  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let j=i+1;j<=n;j++){
      if (str[i-1] == str[j-1] && dp[i-1][j-1] < (j - i)) {
        dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1;
        if (dp[i][j] > maxLen) {
          maxLen = dp[i][j];
          end = i-1;
          lenTemp = maxLen;
          hashMap[lenTemp] = 1;
        } else if (dp[i][j] == maxLen) {
          lenTemp = maxLen;
          hashMap[lenTemp]++;
        }
      } else {
        dp[i][j] = 0;
      }
    }
  }

  if (maxLen > 0) {
    console.log("Longest repeating substring is " + str.substring(end - maxLen + 1, end+1));
  } else {
    console.log("No repeating substring");
  }

  console.log("Count of longest repeating substring is " + hashMap[lenTemp]);
}

//Testing the function
longestRepeatingSubstring("banana");
```

With the input "banana", this script will output:

```
Longest repeating substring is ana
Count of longest repeating substring is 2
```

It finds the repeating substring "ana" and counts it occurs twice in the given string "banana".

