The `is_palindrome` helper function checks whether a given string is the same when read forwards and backwards. This is done by comparing the string with its reverse (`s[::-1]`).

The `get_val` helper function calculates the total value of a string by summing up the position of each letter in the English alphabet. This is done by subtracting the Unicode code point of the letter `'a'` from the Unicode code point of each letter in the string, and then adding 1 (because `'a'` is the first letter, not the zeroth). This ensures that `'a'` contributes 1 to the total, `'b'` contributes 2, and so on.

