The `circularShift` function also handles edge cases such as an empty array and negative shift values by checking for these conditions before performing the shift operation. If the shift number is equal to zero, the array will remain the same, so no shift operation is performed. If the shift number is greater than the size of the array, the shift number is reduced to its modulus with respect to the size of the array to bring the shift number within the size of the array.

