Here's a Python solution that identifies word-level, non-recursive anagrams, either standalone or inter-word. It also identifies palindromes within the text. It does not identify anagrams of non-adjacent words (i.e. words separated by others), or nested anagrams and doesn't apply across paragraphs. Considering all these aspects together, in real large texts, can generating an extreme amount of records and require a lot of computational power and memory to handle.

```python
from collections import defaultdict
import re

def process_text(text):
    return re.sub(r'\W+', ' ', text.lower()).split()

def get_anagrams(words):
    anagrams = defaultdict(list)
    for i, word in enumerate(words):
        key = "".join(sorted(word))
        anagrams[key].append((i, word))
    return {key: value for key, value in anagrams.items() if len(value) > 1}

def get_palindromes(words):
    palindromes = defaultdict(list)
    for i, word in enumerate(words):
        if word == word[::-1]:
            palindromes[word].append(i)
    return palindromes

def find_anagrams_paragraph(paragraph):
    words = process_text(paragraph)
    return get_anagrams(words), get_palindromes(words)

def find_anagrams(text):
    paragraphs = text.split("\n")
    results = []
    for i, paragraph in enumerate(paragraphs):
        anagrams, palindromes = find_anagrams_paragraph(paragraph)
        results.append({"paragraph": i,
                        "anagrams": anagrams,
                        "palindromes": palindromes})
    return results
```

Please note that the time complexity of this code can be approximately considered as O(n^2) because of the loop in `get_anagrams` processing each pair of characters in a word (`sorted`). And the space complexity will also be approximately O(n), where n is the number of unique anagrams in the text, as it stores anagrams and their positions in a dictionary. However, this time complexity doesn't meet the requirements when considering nested anagrams, so an optimized algorithm should be structured. The identification of anagrams and palindromes that span across multiple paragraphs is also a complex problem not considered in this response but that can certainly become a focus of further development.

