The binomial coefficient is calculated using the equation `n! / r!(n - r)!`. For large values of `n` and `r`, this calculation can result in an `OverflowError`, so if this error is encountered, the function uses a more efficient calculation.

The calculation `n! / r!(n - r)!` simplifies to the product of `n-i` divided by `i+1` for `i` from `0` to `r-1`, which is what the `for` loop calculates. This calculation avoids overflowing by doing the division at each step of the multiplication, and by dividing the larger numbers first.

