We then take the first string in the array as a prefix. The subsequent strings are then matched with the prefix from the start. If it does not match, we shorten the prefix by one character from the end until it matches. 

This operation continues until we process all the strings. When we move on to the next string, we already have the longest common prefix of the previous strings, which shortens the matching process. This is an optimized solution, suitable for large arrays, with time complexity of O(N*M) where N is the number of strings and M is the length of the largest string. 

