The GET and POST methods are part of the HTTP protocol, and are used by AJAX for requesting data from the servers.

1. `GET` is used to request data from a specified resource. Data is appended to the URL as parameters. It's a safe method, meaning it can't change the state or data on the server. It's also idempotent, meaning multiple request will have the same effect as one request. 

2. `POST` is used to send data to a server to create/update a resource. The data sent to the server with POST is stored in the request body. POST requests are never cached and do not remain in the browser history.

