}

class SecondComponent extends SecondComponentBase {
    // Implementations or additions specific to `SecondComponent`
}
```
This way, TypeScript enforces that both `FirstComponent` and `SecondComponent` classes have the methods declared in `ComponentBase`. One important thing about this approach is that, as per the DOM specification, you can't directly extend HTML elements, you need to use `customElements.define()`, and it doesn't work in all browsers yet.

