This function will calculate the factorial of the input number `n`. First it checks if the number is negative. If it is, the function returns an error message. The function then checks if `n` is 0 or 1. If it is, the function returns 1 because the factorial of 0 and 1 is 1. It then checks if `n` is an integer. The factorial is only defined for non-negative integers, so if `n` is not an integer, an error message is returned. 

Otherwise, the function recalls itself with the argument `n - 1` and multiplies this result by `n`. This continues until `n` is 0, at which point the recursion stops. 

