1. For speed, if we are to check primes for many numbers, it will be beneficial to pre-compute primes up to a certain number using a method such as Sieve of Eratosthenes, and then directly check for existence.
2. Instead of manually checking every number for primality by iterating through all its divisors, we can improve time efficiency by using probabilistic primality tests.
3. When checking large ranges, make use of parallel processing to speed up computation.

