Then, we need to check if a sqube is prime-proof and includes the substring "200". To do this, we can use a simple brute-force approach: try to replace each digit (or pair of digits, for numbers with more than 10 digits) of a sqube by all possible other digits, check if the result is prime, and if all such numbers are composite, then the sqube is prime-proof.

