In the ternary search function, we first calculate two mid points (mid1 and mid2) that divide the array into three equal parts. If the target number is present at any mid point, we return the mid point. Otherwise, we check in which part the target number can be, and discard the other two parts. 

We repeat this process until the target number is found or the array cannot be divided further. If the target number cannot be found, we return -1.

