- grid-template-areas specifies a grid layout using named grid areas. This allows easier positioning and repositioning of grid items. "header header" places the header across the full width of the grid, "left right" places the 'Left' div on the left and the 'Right' div on the right, and "footer footer" places the footer across the full width of the grid. 
- grid-template-rows sets the height of the grid rows. '10%' creates a row for the header that takes up 10% of the container height, '1fr' creates a row for the 'Left' and 'Right' divs that takes up the remainder of the space, and another '10%' row for the footer.
- grid-template-columns sets the width of the grid columns. '20%' sets the 'Left' div to occupy 20% of the container width, and '80%' for the 'Right' div to occupy the rest of the space.
- The grid-area property assigns an item to a named grid area. The name must match one of the named grid areas specified with grid-template-areas.

This layout works well with CSS Grid because it organizes elements into a set pattern. It also scales nicely to larger screens, as the dimensions are specified relative to the container's height and width. It also reduces the need for positioning hacks or extensive use of margin and padding that was required in the original layout.

