The cocktail_shaker_sort function sorts the array using a variant of bubble sort called cocktail shaker sort (or bidirectional bubble sort). The algorithm works by repeatedly stepping through the list, compares each pair of adjacent items and swaps them if they are in the wrong order. The pass through the list is repeated until no more swaps are needed. The list is then returned in ascending order.

The cocktail_shaker_sort variant of the bubble sort differs in that it sorts in both directions each time through the list. This has the effect of propelling both the smallest and largest unsorted elements to their correct position in one pass. The algorithm continues this process until it makes a pass through the list without swapping any items (indicating that the list is fully sorted). 

Finally, the numbers are printed out in sorted order.

