Here's a PHP program that uses the Dynamic Programming (DP) approach to locate the maximal common subsequence of two specific strings and renders the start index parameter and length of the maximal shared subsequence. Additionally, it includes error handling operations for non-string inputs or empty strings.

```php
<?php
// Function to find maximal shared subsequence
function maximalCommonSubsequence($str1, $str2) {
    // Check if input is not string or is empty
    if (!is_string($str1) || !is_string($str2)) {
        throw new Exception("Input is not a string.\n");
    }
    if ($str1 == "" || $str2 == "") {
        throw new Exception("Input string is empty.\n");
    }

    $len1 = strlen($str1);
    $len2 = strlen($str2);
    $maxLength = 0; //Length of Maximum length common subsequence.
    $row = 0; //To store the index of cell with maximum length subsequence.

    // Matrices to store length of subsequence and to backtrack the subsequence
    $lengthMatrix = array(array());
    $directionMatrix = array(array());

    // Initialization of lengthMatrix
    for ($i = 0; $i <= $len1; $i++) {
        $lengthMatrix[$i][0] = 0;
    }
    for ($j = 0; $j <= $len2; $j++) {
        $lengthMatrix[0][$j] = 0;
    }

    // Compute the length of maximal common substring using DP approach
    for ($i = 1; $i <= $len1; $i++) {
        for ($j = 1; $j <= $len2; $j++) {
            if ($str1[$i - 1] == $str2[$j - 1]) {
                $lengthMatrix[$i][$j] = $lengthMatrix[$i - 1][$j - 1] + 1;
                if ($lengthMatrix[$i][$j] > $maxLength) {
                    $maxLength = $lengthMatrix[$i][$j];
                    $row = $i;
                }
            } else {
                $lengthMatrix[$i][$j] = 0;
            }
        }
    }

    // The start index of the maximal common subsequence
    $start = $row - $maxLength;

    $result = array("start" => $start, "length" => $maxLength);

    return $result;
}

try {
