The function `separateAndCountParenGroups` removes white spaces and splits parentheses groups into array. Then counts each character in each parentheses group. If parenthesis group is balanced (that means the number of '(' is equal to number of ')') it adds to the final groups list.

Note: If you want to count distinct parenthesis only, then you can replace `count++;` inside the `if (char === ')')` block with `if (temp_group[temp_group.length - 1] === '(') count++;`. This will increase the count only if the immediate previous character is '(', i.e., it will not treat '))' as two balanced parenthesis.

