In the selection sort algorithm, the outer loop iterates over each element of the array. The inner loop finds the smallest (or largest, if sorting in descending order) element in the remaining unsorted part of the list. After each complete iteration, it swaps that smallest (or largest) element with the first element of the considered range. This process continues until the array is completely sorted.

Finally, it returns the sorted array. The input list is modified in-place as a result of this algorithm.

