In terms of time complexity, both `findRoot` and `findRootWithConstantSpace` are linear because they iterate through each node once. In terms of space complexity, `findRoot` is linear because it creates a set of child nodes, whereas `findRootWithConstantSpace` is constant, as it only keeps track of two sums, regardless of the number of nodes.

