2. Be registered with SendGrid and have an API Key.
3. Be registered with a stock market data provider and have an API Key.

NPM packages we will use:
- axios: To make HTTP requests to get stock data.
- @sendgrid/mail: To send email via SendGrid

Step 1: Initialize your Node.js project:

```
npm init -y
```

Step 2: Install the necessary packages

```
npm install axios @sendgrid/mail readline-sync
```

Step 3: Now you can create a new file, app.js and paste the following code:

```javascript
const axios = require('axios');
const readline = require('readline-sync');
const mailer = require('@sendgrid/mail');

mailer.setApiKey('Your_SendGrid_API_Key');

const STOCK_API_KEY = 'Your_Stock_API_Key';

function fetchStockDetails(stockName) {
  const url = `https://www.alphavantage.co/query?function=GLOBAL_QUOTE&symbol=${stockName}&apikey=${STOCK_API_KEY}`;
  return axios.get(url)
    .then(response => response.data)
    .catch(error => {
      console.error('Error fetching stock data', error);
      throw error;
    });
}

function sendEmail(mailTo, mailContent) {
  const msg = {
    to: mailTo,
    from: 'your-email@domain.com', // Use your email
    subject: `Stock Market changes for ${mailContent["01. symbol"]}`,
    text: `Stock ${mailContent["01. symbol"]} has an opening price of ${mailContent["02. open"]}, closing price of ${mailContent["08. previous close"]}, traded high at ${mailContent["03. high"]} and low at ${mailContent["04. low"]}. The latest trading volume was ${mailContent["06. volume"]}, listed on the Stock Exchange.`, 
  };

  return mailer.send(msg);
}

const email = readline.question('Enter your email to receive stock market updates: ');
const stockName = readline.question('Enter name of the stock you are interested in: ');

fetchStockDetails(stockName)
  .then(data => {
      sendEmail(email, data["Global Quote"]);
      console.log('Stock market changes email sent successfully.');
  })
  .catch(err =>  console.log('An error occurred', err));
```

Please replace 'Your_SendGrid_API_Key' and 'Your_Stock_API_Key' with your actual API keys. The script will prompt for an email and the stock symbol. It fetches the related stock details and sends an email to the entered email address.

Keep in mind, most free stock API's, including Alpha Vantage used in this example, have a limited amount of requests per minute. 

Also note, for simplicity, it assumes that the provided stock symbol and email address are valid and does not handle every error that may occur during the request or when sending an email. Make sure to use appropriate error handling for your use case.

Also, don't forget to maintain your API keys securely. In this example, I used them directly in the code for simplicity. It's better to use node's environment variables to keep your secrets. 

This simple script can be further expanded with more complex features as per your need.

Lastly, please be aware that sending emails with actual stock data will be subject to regulations in many jurisdictions.

