Creating a three-dimensional spiral array using Java is not a straightforward algorithm. Here's a program for that.

Since the exact manner of the spiral hasn't been described, the following code will treat the 3D array like a series of spiraled 2D arrays (slices) each representing the third "depth" dimension. The slices will be filled in a counter-clockwise spiral. 

```java
public class Spiral3DArray {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int p = 4, q = 4, r = 4;
        int[][][] arr = generate3DArray(p, q, r);
        print3DArray(arr, p, q, r);
    }

    private static int[][][] generate3DArray(int p, int q, int r) {
        int[][][] arr = new int[p][q][r];

        int value = 1;
        for (int s = 0; s < r; s++) {
            int i = 0, j = -1;
            int pi = p, qi = q;
            while (true) {
                for (int a = 0; a < qi; a++) {
                    arr[i][++j][s] = value++;
                }
                if (--pi == 0) break;
                for (int a = 0; a < pi; a++) {
                    arr[++i][j][s] = value++;
                }
                if (--qi == 0) break;
                for (int a = 0; a < qi; a++) {
                    arr[i][--j][s] = value++;
                }
                if (--pi == 0) break;
                for (int a = 0; a < pi; a++) {
                    arr[--i][j][s] = value++;
                }
                if (--qi == 0) break;
            }
        }
        return arr;
    }

    private static void print3DArray(int[][][] arr, int p, int q, int r) {
        for (int k = 0; k < r; k++) {
            System.out.println("Depth " + (k + 1) + ": ");
            for (int i = 0; i < p; i++) {
                for (int j = 0; j < q; j++) {
                    System.out.print(arr[i][j][k] + " ");
                }
                System.out.println();
            }
            System.out.println("-----------------");
        }
    }
}
```

This program will generate a 3D array with the dimensions p x q x r and print the elements of each 3D "slice" in a spiral pattern from the center, moving counterclockwise. Each value will be unique and will range from 1 to p * q * r.
Please note that above script will work as expected when p=q.

