A trendline or line of best fit for a scatter plot is essentially the visual representation of the regression equation for the data. If you have a set of points in a two-dimensional space, the simplest method of calculating the trendline is by using the method of least squares for a linear regression line.

Here is a sample code in C# to compute the linear regression line given a list of points:

```CSharp
public class Point
{
    public double X { get; set; }
    public double Y { get; set; }
}

public static (double slope, double intercept) GetTrendline(List<Point> points)
{
    double xSum = 0;
    double ySum = 0;
    double xySum = 0;
    double xSquareSum = 0;

    foreach (var point in points)
    {
        xSum += point.X;
        ySum += point.Y;
        xySum += point.X * point.Y;
        xSquareSum += point.X * point.X;
    }

    double n = points.Count;
    double slope = ((n * xySum) - (xSum * ySum)) / ((n * xSquareSum) - (xSum * xSum));
    double intercept = (ySum - (slope * xSum)) / n;

    return (slope, intercept);
}
```

If your scatter plot is a chart and you want to plot a trendline, typically you need two points to plot a line. The start and end point of your trendline would then be:

- Start point (x1, y1) = (Minimum x-value, Corresponding y-value on the trendline)
- End point (x2, y2) = (Maximum x-value, Corresponding y-value on the trendline)

Where the corresponding y-value is given by the equation of the line, `y = slope * x + intercept`. You can calculate them as such:

```CSharp
var trendline = GetTrendline(points);
var startPoint = new Point() { X = points.Min(p => p.X), Y = trendline.slope * points.Min(p => p.X) + trendline.intercept };
var endPoint = new Point() { X = points.Max(p => p.X), Y = trendline.slope * points.Max(p => p.X) + trendline.intercept };
