```javascript
function fibonacci(n,memo) {
    memo = memo || {};

    if (memo[n]) {
        return memo[n];
    }
    if (n <= 1) {
        return 1;
    }

    return memo[n] = fibonacci(n - 1, memo) + fibonacci(n - 2, memo);
}

for(let i = 0; i<10; i++){
    console.log(fibonacci(i));
}
```
In the above code, we use a memo object to save the computed values of the Fibonacci numbers as we calculate them. This significantly improves performance for large inputs, as we avoid repeated computations. We then use a for-loop to output the first 10 Fibonacci numbers to the console using the `console.log` function.

