Yes, here is a PHP function that implements the Longest Common Subsequence (LCS) algorithm to find the maximum common subsequence between two strings:

```php
function longestCommonSubsequence($string1, $string2)
{
    $length1 = strlen($string1);
    $length2 = strlen($string2);

    $lengthMatrix = array_fill(0, $length1 + 1, array_fill(0, $length2 + 1, 0));

    for ($i = 1; $i <= $length1; $i++) {
        for ($j = 1; $j <= $length2; $j++) {
            if ($string1[$i - 1] == $string2[$j - 1]) {
                $lengthMatrix[$i][$j] = $lengthMatrix[$i - 1][$j - 1] + 1;
            } else {
                $lengthMatrix[$i][$j] = max($lengthMatrix[$i - 1][$j], $lengthMatrix[$i][$j - 1]);
            }
        }
    }

    $lcs = '';
    $i = $length1; 
    $j = $length2;

    while ($i > 0 && $j > 0) {
        if ($string1[$i - 1] == $string2[$j - 1]) {
            $lcs = $string1[$i - 1] . $lcs; 
            $i--;
            $j--;
        } else if ($lengthMatrix[$i][$j - 1] > $lengthMatrix[$i - 1][$j]) {
            $j--;
        } else {
            $i--;
        }
    }

    return $lcs;
}
```
You can use the function as follows:

```php
$string1 = 'ABCDGH';
$string2 = 'AEDFHR';

echo 'The longest common subsequence is: ' . longestCommonSubsequence($string1, $string2); // The result will be 'ADH'
``` 

This function firstly initializes a length matrix to store the length of common subsequences. Then it iterates through the two strings. If the current characters in both strings match, it adds 1 to the length of the common subsequence without the current characters. If the current characters don't match, it selects the longer subsequence that either ignores the current character of the first string or the current character of the second string.

After calculating the length matrix, the function backtracks from the last character of both strings to obtain the longest common subsequence. If the current characters of both strings match, it can only backtrack diagonally above and to the left. If the current characters don't match, it backtracks to the cell that has a greater value.

The function returns the longest common subsequence of the two input strings.

