            value = 4
        else:
            value = pascal_modified(n-1) + pascal_modified(n-2) + pascal_modified(n-3) + pascal_modified(n-5)
        # store the result
        calculated_values[n] = value
        return value
    return pascal_modified(n)
```
In the above approach, pascal_modified function is the main recursive function which computes the nth number in pascal triangle with the given offset. I've used a dictionary called calculated_values to store already computed values.
Please note that this solution assumes 1 for 0th and 1st element, 2 for the 2nd, 3rd, and 4 for the 4th elements. Then for n > 4, it sums up the (n-1)th, (n-2)nd, (n-3)rd and (n-5)th elements.

