string rfc3339Format = dt.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss.fffzzz", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
```
This will output something like '2021-09-21T14:37:00.123-07:00' for a certain DateTime instance.

The RFC 3339 formatted string specifies fractions of seconds ('fff') and uses the local offset from Coordinated Universal Time (UTC, 'zzz').

To convert a RFC 3339 formatted string back to a DateTime object you can use DateTime.ParseExact (or DateTime.TryParseExact for a safer version that doesn't throw exceptions):

