if(DateTime.TryParseExact(rfc3339String, "yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss.fffzzz", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.AdjustToUniversal, out dt)){
    // do something with dt
} else {
    // handle invalid format
}
```
In this example, the input string '2021-09-21T14:37:00.123-07:00' is parsed back to a DateTime instance. The DateTimeStyles.AdjustToUniversal option is used to adjust the parsed date-time value to a UTC DateTime.

Note: RFC 3339 requires that times are expressed either in UTC or a local time with timezone. It does not allow for expressions in local time without time zone. The examples above cover local times with an explicit time zone offset. If you have a DateTime in UTC, you can use the 'Z' designator :

