Here is a sample implementation for the given problem where our aim is to insert nodes, delete nodes, find a node, calculate product of all node values, and perform an in-order tree traversal.

```java
public class Node {
  double value;
  Node left;
  Node right;

  Node(double value) {
    this.value = value;
    right = null;
    left = null;
  }
}

public class BinaryTree {
  Node root;

  BinaryTree() {
    root = null;
  }

  // insert method
  public void add(double value) {
    root = addRecursive(root, value);
  }

  private Node addRecursive(Node current, double value) {
    if (current == null) {
      return new Node(value);
    }

    if (value < current.value) {
      current.left = addRecursive(current.left, value);
    } else if (value > current.value) {
      current.right = addRecursive(current.right, value);
    }

    return current;
  }

  // find node method
  public boolean containsNode(double value) {
    return containsNodeRecursive(root, value);
  }

  private boolean containsNodeRecursive(Node current, double value) {
    if (current == null) {
      return false;
    } 

    if (value == current.value) {
      return true;
    } 

    return value < current.value
      ? containsNodeRecursive(current.left, value)
      : containsNodeRecursive(current.right, value);
  }

  // calculate product
  public double calculateProduct(){
    return calculateProductRecursive(root);
  }

  private double calculateProductRecursive(Node node){
    if(node == null)
      return 1;
    else 
      return(node.value * calculateProductRecursive(node.left) * calculateProductRecursive(node.right));
  }

  // In-order tree traversal
  void printInorder(Node node) { 
    if (node == null) 
      return; 

    printInorder(node.left); 

    System.out.print(node.value + " "); 

    printInorder(node.right); 
  } 

  // Delete a node
  public void delete(double value) {
    root = deleteRecursive(root, value);
  }

  private Node deleteRecursive(Node current, double value) {
    if (current == null) {
      return null;
    }

    if (value == current.value) {
      // Node to delete found

      if (current.left == null && current.right == null) {
        return null;
      }

      if (current.right == null) {
        return current.left;
      }

      if (current.left == null) {
        return current.right;
      }

      // The node has two children, 
      // move the rightmost node in the left subtree to current
      double rightmostValue = findRightmostValue(current.left);
      current.value = rightmostValue;
      current.left = deleteRecursive(current.left, rightmostValue);
      return current;

    } 
    if (value < current.value) {
      current.left = deleteRecursive(current.left, value);
      return current;
    }

    current.right = deleteRecursive(current.right, value);
    return current;
  }

  private double findRightmostValue(Node node) {
    return node.right == null ? node.value : findRightmostValue(node.right);
  }
}
```

This code first creates a node class and a binary tree class. The node class has a value, and a right and left node. The binary tree class has the root node of the tree and methods to add a new node, delete a node, find if a node exists in the tree, calculate the product of all nodes, and an in-order traversal. It uses recursion for these operations.

