    }
  }
}
```

In this code:

- A BufferedImage object is used to work with images in Java.
- A Graphics2D object is created from the output image, which allows us to "draw" the input image onto the output image in a scaled manner (resizes the image).
- The drawImage method is used to draw the transformed (scaled) input image into the output image.
- `GaussianBlur` class from JavaFX API is used to blur the image.

Remember: Image processing in Java is more verbose & complex than in Python, because many operations that are simple function calls in Python require direct manipulation of pixel data in Java. JavaFX api provides many additional imaging capabilities and should be explored.

